From: Local diagnostic candidate
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu/uvd3.1: check the status register before validating

The already-validated guard tests a UVD_FW_STATUS flag against UVD_FW_START,
which contains the firmware key selection. Read UVD_FW_STATUS instead, matching
the later validation-result check in the same function. This avoids repeating
validation solely because the key-selection value lacks the PASS bit.

Candidate for the observed MacBookPro11,5 s2idle UVD resume failure. Hardware
validation is pending; this does not claim to fix the separate deep-S3 gfx
ring timeout. Preserve actual firmware validation when PASS is not set.

Related upstream commit: 13e4cf116dbf7a1fb8123a59bea2c098f30d3736
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/uvd_v3_1.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/uvd_v3_1.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/uvd_v3_1.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/uvd_v3_1.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/uvd_v3_1.c
@@ -288,7 +288,7 @@ static int uvd_v3_1_fw_validate(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 	int i;
 	uint32_t keysel = adev->uvd.keyselect;
 
-	if (RREG32(mmUVD_FW_START) & UVD_FW_STATUS__PASS_MASK) {
+	if (RREG32(mmUVD_FW_STATUS) & UVD_FW_STATUS__PASS_MASK) {
 		dev_dbg(adev->dev, "UVD keyselect already set: 0x%x (on CPU: 0x%x)\n",
 			RREG32(mmUVD_FW_START), adev->uvd.keyselect);
 		return 0;
